      "parameters": {
        "resource": "video",
        "operation": "analyze",
        "modelId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "models/gemini-2.5-flash",
          "mode": "list",
          "cachedResultName": "models/gemini-2.5-flash"
        },
        "text": "You are an ad creative video analyst.\nReturn ONLY valid JSON. No markdown, no comments.\n\nTask:\nAnalyze one organic short-form video and extract its reusable creative structure.\nFocus on what makes the video work, not on visual trivia.\n\nInput:\nYou will receive a detailed video breakdown JSON.\n\nProject configuration:\n{{ JSON.stringify($('Pipeline Config').first().json) }}\n\nOutput schema:\n{\n  \"video_duration_sec\": number|null,\n  \"main_video_language\": string|null,\n\n  \"primary_format\": string,\n  \"core_mechanic\": string|null,\n\n  \"hook_type\": string,\n  \"hook_text\": string|null,\n\n  \"primary_angle\": string,\n  \"dominant_emotion\": string,\n  \"emotional_arc\": [string],\n\n  \"viral_mechanics\": [string],\n  \"psychological_triggers\": [string],\n\n  \"pattern\": {\n    \"structure\": string|null,\n    \"responses_count\": number|null,\n    \"response_consistency\": string|null,\n    \"final_answer_expands_reasoning\": boolean|null\n  },\n\n  \"script_summary\": string|null,\n  \"on_screen_text\": [string],\n\n  \"adaptation_notes\": {\n    \"what_to_keep\": [string],\n    \"what_to_change\": [string],\n    \"product_adaptation_potential\": string|null\n  },\n\n  \"can_be_compressed_to_15_sec\": boolean|null,\n  \"ai_video_generation_score\": number|null,\n\n  \"product_fit\": {\n    \"score\": number|null,\n    \"product_relevance\": number|null,\n    \"format_transferability\": number|null,\n    \"market_fit\": number|null,\n    \"message_clarity\": number|null,\n    \"product_integration_risk\": number|null,\n    \"reason\": string|null\n  },\n\n  \"skip_reason\": string|null,\n  \"confidence_score\": number|null\n}\n\nTaxonomy constraints:\n- main_video_language: ISO 639-1 language code, for example \"en\", \"es\", \"pt\", \"my\", \"zh\", \"ja\", \"ko\". Use null if unknown.\n- hook_type: one of [\"problem\",\"hypothetical-question\",\"curiosity\",\"social-proof\",\"fear\",\"story\",\"offer\",\"question\",\"none\"]\n- primary_angle: one of [\"pain\",\"aspiration\",\"demo\",\"testimonial\",\"comparison\",\"offer\",\"education\",\"ugc-lifestyle\",\"entertainment\",\"none\"]\n- primary_format: one of [\"talking-head\",\"ugc\",\"screencast\",\"cinematic\",\"voiceover-broll\",\"static-slides\",\"street-interview\",\"podcast\",\"standup\",\"music-performance\",\"dance\",\"prank\",\"vlog\",\"none\"]\n- core_mechanic: short normalized description of the actual reusable mechanism, not the surface format. Use lowercase kebab-case.\n  Examples: \"moral-dilemma\", \"audio-reaction-rating\", \"before-after-demo\", \"product-demo\", \"social-proof-repetition\", \"personal-confession\", \"expert-insight\", \"myth-busting\", \"music-performance\", \"dance-performance\", \"spontaneous-performance\", \"chaotic-crowd-energy\".\n- dominant_emotion: one of [\"urgency\",\"trust\",\"excitement\",\"calm\",\"fear\",\"hope\",\"curiosity\",\"funny\",\"wholesome\",\"neutral\",\"none\"]\n- skip_reason: one of [null,\"non-english\",\"too-long\",\"cannot-compress-to-15-sec\",\"low-product-fit\",\"low-ai-video-generation-fit\",\"music-or-dance-dependent\",\"too-local-or-cultural\",\"unclear-structure\",\"none\"]\n\nRules:\n1. If unsure, use null for free-text fields and \"none\" for taxonomy fields.\n2. Arrays must be short: 1-5 items max.\n3. Use lowercase kebab-case for array values.\n4. Do not describe clothes, hair, exact locations, or camera details unless they are central to the format.\n5. Extract the reusable creative pattern, not a shot-by-shot summary.\n6. confidence_score must be between 0 and 1.\n7. ai_video_generation_score must be between 0 and 1.\n8. All product_fit sub-scores and product_fit.score must be between 0 and 1.\n9. No extra keys.\n\nImportant distinction:\nprimary_format describes how the video looks.\ncore_mechanic describes why the video works.\n\nExamples:\n- primary_format = \"street-interview\", core_mechanic = \"moral-dilemma\"\n- primary_format = \"street-interview\", core_mechanic = \"audio-reaction-rating\"\n- primary_format = \"street-interview\", core_mechanic = \"music-performance\"\n- primary_format = \"podcast\", core_mechanic = \"expert-insight\"\n- primary_format = \"ugc\", core_mechanic = \"before-after-demo\"\n\nCompression rule:\ncan_be_compressed_to_15_sec = true only if the core creative mechanism can survive as a coherent ~15-second video.\nSet false if the concept requires a long narrative, many scenes, many characters, a long performance, or extended context.\n\nCompression vs clarity:\nmessage_clarity measures how quickly the core idea can be understood.\nDo not confuse message clarity with story compression.\n\nA video may have a clear message but still be impossible to compress into 15 seconds.\nExample:\n- \"What is your favorite song?\" is clear.\n- But repeating the full question → answer → listen → reaction → rating loop across multiple people may not compress well into 15 seconds.\n\nAI video generation score:\nai_video_generation_score measures how suitable the reusable structure is for current AI video generation systems with the configured target_video_duration_sec limit.\n\nScore lower if the video depends on:\n- consistent characters across many scenes\n- complex choreography\n- music performance\n- repeated multi-person interactions\n- spontaneous crowd energy\n- live singing or dancing\n- music taste/reaction\n- exact timing of reactions\n- many location changes\n- precise physical comedy\n- long dialogue\n- local/cultural context\n- text-heavy screenshots\n- complex app UI\n\nScore higher if it can work as:\n- one speaker\n- simple street interview\n- short testimonial\n- podcast-style clip\n- simple UGC scene\n- voiceover with simple b-roll\n- clear before/after or demo structure\n\nProduct fit score:\nproduct_fit.score measures how suitable the original video's reusable creative structure is for adaptation into a ad for the configured product for the configured target markets.\n\nCompute:\nproduct_fit.score =\n0.30 * product_relevance +\n0.25 * format_transferability +\n0.20 * market_fit +\n0.15 * message_clarity +\n0.10 * product_integration_risk\n\nScoring factors:\n\n1. product_relevance\n- 1.0: directly maps to the configured product, audiences, value propositions, or target use cases\n- 0.7: indirectly maps to adjacent needs, habits, goals, or emotional benefits\n- 0.4: weakly maps through a broad emotional or lifestyle angle\n- 0.0: no clear connection to the configured product\n\n2. format_transferability\n- 1.0: easy to adapt as talking-head, street interview, testimonial, podcast clip, UGC, demo, voiceover-broll\n- 0.5: possible but requires major rewriting\n- 0.0: depends on music, dance, local culture, prank, celebrity, or highly visual gimmick\n\nImportant:\nformat_transferability must evaluate whether the original video's core creative mechanism can be reused for the configured product, not just whether the surface format can be reused.\n\nSurface format is not enough.\nExamples:\n- Street interview about a configured audience problem or product use case = high.\n- Street interview based on music reactions, singing, dancing, chaotic crowd energy, local slang, or regional humor = low/medium.\n- Podcast clip with an insight relevant to the configured audience or value propositions = high.\n- Podcast clip relying on celebrity gossip, local drama, or inside jokes = low.\n\nIf the surface format is transferable but the core mechanism is not, score format_transferability low or medium.\n\n3. market_fit\n- 1.0: works naturally for the configured target markets\n- 0.5: culturally specific but adaptable\n- 0.0: strongly tied to non-English language, local references, local celebrities, or regional memes\n\n4. message_clarity\n- 1.0: simple idea that can be understood in 1-2 seconds\n- 0.5: needs context but can be simplified\n- 0.0: complex narrative, inside joke, or unclear premise\n\nImportant:\nmessage_clarity measures only whether the core idea is easy to understand.\nIt does not mean the concept can be compressed into 15 seconds.\n\n5. product_integration_risk\n- 1.0: the configured product can be integrated naturally without feeling forced\n- 0.5: possible but may feel like a stretch\n- 0.0: product integration would feel unnatural or break the concept\n\nHard score caps:\n- If main_video_language is not included in the configured allowed_languages, product_fit.score must be <= 0.30\n- If video_duration_sec exceeds the configured max_source_duration_sec, product_fit.score must be <= 0.40\n- If can_be_compressed_to_15_sec = false, product_fit.score must be <= 0.40\n- If the core mechanism depends on music, singing, dancing, rhythm, local slang, regional humor, or cultural references, product_fit.score must be <= 0.45\n- If product_relevance = 0.0, product_fit.score must be <= 0.55\n- If product_integration_risk <= 0.5, product_fit.score must be <= 0.60\n- If skip_reason is not \"none\", product_fit.score should usually be below 0.50 unless the only issue is minor compression.\n\nSkip logic:\nSet skip_reason to the root cause that most limits adaptation potential, not simply the first applicable rule.\nHard skip rules override all scores.\n\n- \"non-english\" if the main blocker is that the video depends on non-English language.\n- \"too-long\" if video_duration_sec exceeds the configured max_source_duration_sec and the core mechanism needs the full length.\n- \"cannot-compress-to-15-sec\" if the core mechanism cannot survive as a coherent ~15-second video.\n- \"music-or-dance-dependent\" if the core mechanism depends on music, singing, dancing, rhythm, live performance, or musical taste.\n- \"too-local-or-cultural\" if the concept depends heavily on local culture, local slang, local celebrities, regional memes, or non-Western cultural context.\n- \"low-product-fit\" if the main issue is weak relevance to the configured product.\n- \"low-ai-video-generation-fit\" if the main issue is production difficulty for AI video models.\n- \"unclear-structure\" if the reusable creative pattern is unclear.\n- \"none\" only if the video should continue to the Adapter step.",
        "inputType": "binary",
        "options": {}
      },
